{
  "openapi": "3.0.1",
  "info": {
    "title": "Octopi API",
    "description": "\n<h2 id=\"octopi_is_a_modern_terminal_operating_system_tos\">Octopi is a modern Terminal Operating System (TOS).</h2>\n\n<h3 id=\"rest__hypermedia\">REST &amp; Hypermedia</h3>\n\n<p>The Octopi API is a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Representational_state_transfer\">RESTful API</a> using JSON and the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HATEOAS\">HATEOAS paradigm</a>. In every JSON response from the API, you will find a list of actions returned as a JSON array. These actions are all the methods available on the API resource. We encourage you to build your clients to use these actions dynamically. That way, if the API changes URLs, your client will keep functioning without changing the source code of your client application.</p>\n\n<h3 id=\"authentication\">Authentication</h3>\n\n<p>The Octopi API uses <a href=\"https://tools.ietf.org/html/draft-hammer-http-token-auth-01\">HTTP Token Access Authentication</a>.</p>\n\n<p>To authenticate, you need to pass in your API Key (obtained from the Octopi Team) in the HTTP request header using an \u2018Authorization\u2019 header with the API key as a token. For example, the header should have \u201cToken token=yourapikey\u201d.</p>\n\n<h3 id=\"dates_and_times\">Dates and Times</h3>\n\n<p>The Octopi API returns all dates and times in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601\">ISO 8601</a> format and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coordinated_Universal_Time\">UTC</a>.</p>\nKaleris",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "x-copyright": "Kaleris",
    "x-jentic-source-url": "https://api.swaggerhub.com/apis/Navis.com/octopi/1.0.0"
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "https://app.octopi.co/api/v1"
    }
  ],
  "tags": [
    {
      "name": "appointments",
      "description": "     This resource allows clients to fetch the available appointment slots, list, view, create, update, reschedule, and cancel appointments in Octopi.'\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "containers",
      "description": "      In Octopi, a container object can represent a container, but sometimes can also represent non-containerized cargo such as break-bulk cargo,\n      cars, boats, etc.\n\n      When a container object has a number, it is a container. When the number is left blank, it represents another type of cargo such as vehicle, breakbulk, boat, etc.\n\n      Containers have many movements. A movement can be a Gate In, Gate Out, Full Stripping, Container Damage, Unloading, etc.\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "freight_forwarders",
      "description": "Use this API resource to CRUD freight forwarders."
    },
    {
      "name": "invoices",
      "description": "      In Octopi, the following three types of invoices can be created:\n      * A pro-forma invoice for a Bill of Lading. These invoices is generally for consignees (importers or exporters). It shows how much they need to pay to retrieve a container from the terminal.\n      * An invoice for a container movement. Any container movement in Octopi can generate an invoice if there is a tariff tied to this event type. For example, a tariff can be created for all 'Gate Out Full' so that every time a container gates out full out of the terminal, an invoice is created for the consignee to which this container is being delivered to.\n      * An invoice for a voyage. An invoice can be generated to charge the shipping lines for the vessel operations and/or container storage following a voyage.\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "movements",
      "description": "      In Octopi, the following types of movements can be created.\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "pre_advices",
      "description": "      This resource allows clients to view, create and delete pre-advices in Octopi\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "shipping_lines",
      "description": "This resource allows you to create, read, update, or delete shipping lines in Octopi."
    },
    {
      "name": "ships",
      "description": "      This API allows you to fetch information about vessels in Octopi. It returns the basic info about the vessel.\n      If the vessel recently completed a voyage, then it also returns information about that last voyage.\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "truck_drivers",
      "description": "This resource lets clients find, create, update or list truck drivers truck driver information."
    },
    {
      "name": "truck_visits",
      "description": "      This resource allows clients to view or manipulate truck visits within Ocotpi.\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "trucking_companies",
      "description": "Use this API resources to CRUD trucking companies."
    },
    {
      "name": "trucks",
      "description": "Use this API resources to CRUD trucks."
    },
    {
      "name": "vessel_tallies",
      "description": "      This resource allows you to view and update vessel tallies in Octopi.\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "voyage_event_types",
      "description": "      This resource allows clients to read voyage event types available for the organization.\n      Voyage event types define the different kinds of events that can occur during a voyage.\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "voyages",
      "description": "This resource allows you to create, read, update, or delete voyages in Octopi."
    },
    {
      "name": "work_queues",
      "description": "      In Octopi, there are different types of work queues:\n      * terminal: where items are created as containers enter and leave the terminal via the gates\n      * voyage: where items are created as containers get unloaded and loaded from vessels.\n      * general_cargo: where items are created as non-containerized cargo enter and leave the terminal via the gates.\n      * warehouse: where items are created as cargo is stripped from a container.\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "cargoes-holds",
      "description": "Octopi allows holds to be placed on cargo.\n\nA terminal operator can created has many hold types as possible to automatically\nor manually create holds on cargo.\n\nHolds can be placed on cargo. When a cargo has a hold, it cannot be delivered to\nthe customer (via a gate movement or a cargo stripping) or loaded on a vessel\nfor export.\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "containers-damages",
      "description": "Octopi allows damages to be reported on containers.\n\nA user can report as many damages as needed for a container.\n\nWhen a container is reported as damaged, it cannot leave the terminal\nuntil the repair is completed.\nNotification emails will be sent for these events based on the organization settings.\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "containers-extra_attributes",
      "description": "This resource allows you modify extra_attributes for containers in Octopi."
    },
    {
      "name": "containers-flex_fields",
      "description": "\\[DEPRECATED\\] Please use the Containers API to manage flex flex fields for containers.\nThis resource allows you to access flex fields for containers in Octopi\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "containers-holds",
      "description": "Octopi allows holds to be placed on containers.\n\nA terminal operator can created has many hold types as possible to automatically\nor manually create holds on containers.\n\nHolds can be placed on containers. When a container has a hold, it cannot be\ndelivered to the customer (via a gate movement or a container stripping) or\nloaded on a vessel for export.\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "containers-tags",
      "description": "      This resource allows you to apply tags to containers in Octopi.\n      If the tag doesn't exist in Octopi, it will be created.\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "containers-terminal_services",
      "description": "      Terminal service can be applied to any container.\n      It also can have a custom value and record of start and end times.\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "containers-weights",
      "description": "      This resource allows you to report the container gross weight in Octopi.\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "general_cargoes-flex_fields",
      "description": "\\[DEPRECATED\\] Please use the General Cargo API to manage flex flex fields for general cargo.\nThis resource allows you to access flex fields for general cargo in Octopi\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "general_cargoes-terminal_services",
      "description": "      Terminal service can be applied to general cargo.\n      It also can have a custom value and record of start and end times.\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "general_cargoes-weights",
      "description": "      This resource allows you to report the general cargo gross weight in Octopi.\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "truck_visits-dock_receipts",
      "description": "      This resource allows clients to view, create, and delete a dock receipts for truck visits in Octopi.\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "truck_visits-general_cargo_deliveries",
      "description": "      This resource allows clients to view, create, and delete a general cargo deliveries for truck visits in Octopi.\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "truck_visits-interchanges",
      "description": "      This resource allows clients to view, create, and delete a interchange for truck visits in Octopi.\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "voyages-flex_fields",
      "description": "\\[DEPRECATED\\] Please use the Containers API to manage flex flex fields for voyages.\nThis resource allows you to access flex fields for voyages in Octopi\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "voyages-voyage_events",
      "description": "      This resource allows clients to create, read, update, and delete voyage events for specific voyages.\n      Voyage events represent different activities or milestones that occur during a voyage.\n\n      Voyage events support flex fields, which allow you to store custom data specific to your organization's needs.\n      Flex fields are passed as an array of key-value pairs using canonical field names in requests, and returned\n      as label-value pairs in responses.\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "work_queues-work_queue_items",
      "description": "      Octopi has many work queues per organization. You can create work queue items for a work queue using this API method.\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "manifests-bill_of_ladings-flex_fields",
      "description": "Customizable fields for Bill of Ladings"
    },
    {
      "name": "manifests-bill_of_ladings-holds",
      "description": "      This resource allows you to view holds that are associated to a specific bill of lading.\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "shipping_lines-bookings-flex_fields",
      "description": "This resource allows you to access flex fields for bookings in Octopi"
    },
    {
      "name": "voyages-bill_of_ladings-hold_types",
      "description": "      This resource allows you to lift and apply holds based on a hold type for all the cargo on a bill of lading.\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "voyages-bill_of_ladings-holds",
      "description": "      This resource allows you to view, lift and apply holds to all the cargo for a specific bill of lading.\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "shipping_lines-bookings-line_items-flex_fields",
      "description": "Allows you to modify flex fields for booking line items in Octopi."
    }
  ],
  "paths": {
    "/appointments": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "appointments"
        ],
        "description": "Returns all the appointments present for a provided date.",
        "operationId": "get_appointments",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "appointment_date",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "Filter appointments for the provided date. Must be formatted as YYYY-MM-DD.",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "appointment_number",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "Filter appointments for a given appointment. You can pass the appointment Octopi ID or the appointment number.",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "terminal",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "Filter appointments for the provided Terminal Name. You can pass the terminal Octopi ID or the terminal name.",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "container",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "Filter appointments associated with a container. You can pass the container Octopi ID or the container number.",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "truck",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "Filter appointments associated with a truck. You can pass the truck Octopi ID or the truck's license plate.",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "bill_of_lading",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "Filter appointments associated with a bill of lading. You can pass the bill of lading Octopi ID or the bill_of_lading number",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "shipping_line",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "Filter appointments associated with a shipping line. You can pass the shipping line Octopi ID or the shiping line's name",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "status",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "Filter appointments for the given status",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "pending",
                "completed",
                "cancelled"
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "booking",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "Filter appointments associated with a booking. You can pass the booking Octopi ID or the booking number",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "purpose",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "Filter appointments for the provided purpose type",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "drop_off",
                "pick_up"
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "delivery_order",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "Filter appointments associated with a delivery order. You can pass the delivery orde Octopi ID or the delivery orde number",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "truck_driver",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "Filter appointments associated with a truck driver. You can pass the truck driver Octopi ID or the truck driver's license number",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "page",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "Specify which page of results to fetch. This value defaults to 1.",
            "schema": {
              "type": "number"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "per",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "The number of appointments to be displayed. This value defaults to 10 and accepts a maximum of 100.",
            "schema": {
              "type": "number"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "404": {
            "description": "Not found.",
            "content": {}
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "Unprocessable Entity.",
            "content": {}
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Internal Server Error.",
            "content": {}
          }
        }
      },
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "appointments"
        ],
        "description": "Creates a new appointment.",
        "operationId": "post_appointments",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "required": [
                  "truck_license"
                ],
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                  "appointment_slot_id": {
                    "type": "number",
                    "description": "Specify the appointment slot to which you want to create the appointment. Either appointment_slot_id or appointment_date_time is mandatory for creating an appointment."
                  },
                  "appointment_date_time": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "The date and time at which you want to book the appointment for, in ISO 8601 format (Eg 2023-08-18T14:00:00Z) in UTC. Either appointment_date_time or appointment_slot_id is mandatory for creating an appointment."
                  },
                  "terminal": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "The name of the terminal to which you want to create the appointment. Terminal is mandatory if there are multiple active terminals present for your organization and you are passing the appointment_date_time instead of appointment_slot_id."
                  },
                  "appointment_number": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Unique appointment number. Should be at least 4 characters. Octopi will auto-generate one if not provided."
                  },
                  "truck_license": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Truck's license plate number."
                  },
                  "truck_driver_id": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Truck driver ID. If this parameter is present, the truck_driver_license parameter will be ignored."
                  },
                  "truck_driver_license": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Truck driver's license number. If the truck_driver_id parameter is present, this will be ignored."
                  },
                  "trucking_company": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "The trucking company for this appointment. If a truck is present, then the trucking company in this parameter must match it. Similarly, if a truck driver is present, the driver's company must match this trucking company."
                  },
                  "comment": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Comments for this appointment."
                  },
                  "purposes": {
                    "type": "array",
                    "description": "Truck visit's purposes (multiple purposes allowed).",
                    "items": {
                      "type": "string"
                    }
                  }
                },
                "additionalProperties": false
              }
            }
          },
          "required": false
        },
        "responses": {
          "404": {
            "description": "Not found.",
            "content": {}
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "Unprocessable Entity.",
            "content": {}
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Internal Server Error.",
            "content": {}
          }
        },
        "x-codegen-request-body-name": "body"
      }
    },
    "/appointments/{appointment_number}": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "appointments"
        ],
        "description": "Returns information about a specific appointment.",
        "operationId": "get_appointments_appointment_number",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "appointment_number",
            "in": "path",
            "description": "The Appointment's number.",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "404": {
            "description": "Not found.",
            "content": {}
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "Unprocessable Entity.",
            "content": {}
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Internal Server Error.",
            "content": {}
          }
        }
      },
      "put": {
        "tags": [
          "appointments"
        ],
        "description": "Updates the fields of an existing appointment and/or reschedule an appointment.",
        "operationId": "put_appointments_appointment_number",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "appointment_number",
            "in": "path",
            "description": "The appointment's number.",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                  "appointment_slot_id": {
                    "type": "number",
                    "description": "Specify the new appointment slot to which you want to reschedule the appointment to. Either appointment_slot_id or appointment_date_time is mandatory for rescheduling an appointment."
                  },
                  "appointment_date_time": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "The date and time at which you want to reschedule the appointment for, in ISO 8601 format (Eg 2023-08-18T14:00:00Z) in UTC. Either appointment_date_time or appointment_slot_id is mandatory for rescheduling an appointment."
                  },
                  "terminal": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "The name of the terminal to which you want to reschedule the appointment. Terminal is mandatory if there are multiple active terminals present for your organization and you are passing the appointment_date_time instead of appointment_slot_id."
                  },
                  "reschedule_reason": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "The reason for rescheduling the appointment. Required if you want to reschedule the appointment."
                  },
                  "truck_license": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Truck's license plate number."
                  },
                  "truck_driver_id": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Truck driver ID. If this parameter is present, the truck_driver_license parameter will be ignored."
                  },
                  "truck_driver_license": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Truck driver's license number. If the truck_driver_id parameter is present, this will be ignored."
                  },
                  "trucking_company": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "The trucking company for this appointment. If a truck is present, then the trucking company in this parameter must match it. Similarly, if a truck driver is present, the driver's company must match this trucking company."
                  },
                  "comment": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Comments for this appointment."
                  },
                  "purposes": {
                    "type": "array",
                    "description": "Truck visit's purposes (multiple purposes allowed). The purposes provided in this API will override the existing purposes in that appointment.",
                    "items": {
                      "type": "string"
                    }
                  }
                },
                "additionalProperties": false
              }
            }
          },
          "required": false
        },
        "responses": {
          "404": {
            "description": "Not found.",
            "content": {}
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "Unprocessable Entity.",
            "content": {}
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Internal Server Error.",
            "content": {}
          }
        },
        "x-codegen-request-body-name": "body"
      }
    },
    "/appointments/{appointment_number}/cancel": {
      "put": {
        "tags": [
          "appointments"
        ],
        "description": "Cancels the appointment",
        "operationId": "put_appointments_appointment_number_cancel",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "appointment_number",
            "in": "path",
            "description": "The appointment's number",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "required": [
                  "cancellation_reason"
                ],
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                  "cancellation_reason": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "The reason for cancelling the appointment"
                  }
                },
                "additionalProperties": false
              }
            }
          },
          "required": false
        },
        "responses": {
          "404": {
            "description": "Not found.",
            "content": {}
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "Unprocessable Entity.",
            "content": {}
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Internal Server Error.",
            "content": {}
          }
        },
        "x-codegen-request-body-name": "body"
      }
    },
    "/appointments/appointment_slots": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "appointments"
        ],
        "description": "Returns all the appointment slots with availablity for a given date.",
        "operationId": "get_appointments_appointment_slots",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "appointment_date",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "Date for which you want the appointment slot details for. Must be formatted as YYYY-MM-DD.",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "terminal",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "The name of the terminal for which you want the appointment slots for. Terminal is mandatory if there are multiple active terminals present for your organization.",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "404": {
            "description": "Not found.",
            "content": {}
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "Unprocessable Entity.",
            "content": {}
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Internal Server Error.",
            "content": {}
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/average_truck_visit_durations.json": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "average_truck_visit_durations"
        ],
        "summary": "Gets a list of average truck visit durations",
        "description": "Every day, Octopi keeps track of the average time a truck spends at a terminal.\nThis API endpoint allows you to access these daily average truck visit duration logs.\n",
        "operationId": "get_average_truck_visit_durations.json",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "terminal_id",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "Filter for a specific terminal. You must pass the terminal's Octopi ID.",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "start_date",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "Filter for days after the start date. Must be formatted as YYYY-MM-DD.",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "end_date",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "Filter for days before the end date. Must be formatted as YYYY-MM-DD.",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "page",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "Specify which page of results to fetch. This value defaults to 1.",
            "schema": {
              "type": "number"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "per",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "The number of items to be displayed. This value defaults to 10 and accepts a maximum of 100.",
            "schema": {
              "type": "number"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "404": {
            "description": "Not found.",
            "content": {}
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "Invalid request.",
            "content": {}
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Internal server error.",
            "content": {}
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/bill_of_ladings.json": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "bill_of_ladings"
        ],
        "summary": "Returns a list of bill of ladings.",
        "operationId": "get_bill_of_ladings.json",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "bl_number",
